Higher salaries can improve teacher retention by making the profession more attractive, reducing the need for constant recruitment and training.
Research shows that better pay is linked to lower turnover, which stabilizes classrooms and supports consistent student learning.
When teachers are fairly compensated, they are more likely to stay in their roles, leading to better long-term educational outcomes for students.
Competitive salaries can help address the imbalance in the education sector by encouraging experienced educators to remain in the field.
Investing in teacher salaries is a cost-effective way to reduce turnover, as replacing teachers is expensive and disruptive.